Name: UniKey Vietnamese input engine (ukengine)
Short Name: unikey
URL: https://github.com/fcitx/fcitx5-unikey
Version: 53f82a1e01dc0484f46dc8ed419d586cebd2f114
Date: 2026-08-15
Revision: 53f82a1e01dc0484f46dc8ed419d586cebd2f114
License: LGPL-2.0-or-later
License File: LICENSE
Security Critical: yes
Shipped: yes

Description:
UniKey's Vietnamese input engine ("ukengine") — a linguistic state machine that
turns a stream of Telex/VNI/VIQR keystrokes into committed Vietnamese Unicode. It
does word-level tone placement (classic "hòa" vs modern "hoà"), spelling
validation, and automatic restoration of words that turn out not to be Vietnamese
(e.g. "congas" typed in Telex stays "congas" instead of being mangled to "congá").
It is vendored to back a new UnikeyEngine behind the ChromeOS IME service's
mojom::InputMethod seam, replacing the stateless rule-based transliterator for the
Vietnamese layouts. Rationale and defect analysis:
internal-knowledge/VIETNAMESE-IME-PERF.md.

colorburst PoC status: this is a proof-of-concept vendoring. The engine core
compiles standalone and is proven correct host-side (see poc_driver.cc). The mojo
adapter lives in chromeos/ash/services/ime/unikey_engine.*.

Local Modifications:
Only the LGPL-2.0-or-later engine core is taken. The GPL-2.0-or-later files of the
upstream tree (charset.cpp, data.cpp, convert.cpp, byteio.cpp, pattern.cpp,
keycons.h, vnconv.h, and the fcitx5 glue unikeyinputcontext.*) are NOT vendored.
Files taken verbatim from upstream (unchanged, LGPL-2.0-or-later):
  - ukengine.cpp, ukengine.h   (the state machine)
  - inputproc.cpp, inputproc.h (key -> linguistic-event classifier; Telex/VNI/...)
  - mactab.h                   (macro-table interface; gõ tắt)
  - vnlexi.h                   (the Vietnamese lexical alphabet enum)

Files added by colorburst to sever the GPL coupling (all authored by us, and, so
that they may be freely combined with the LGPL engine, released under
LGPL-2.0-or-later):
  - keycons.h        clean-room reimplementation of the upstream GPL keycons.h:
                     only the interface constants/enums/option struct the engine
                     needs (functional API, rewritten from the public surface).
  - charset.h        minimal shim: the StdVnChar encoding, a tiny UTF-8 output
                     stream+charset object, the two fold tables, and stubs for the
                     macro-only VnConvert. Replaces the GPL charset.h/byteio.h/
                     vnconv.h. The single output charset emits UTF-8 directly, so
                     the whole legacy TCVN/VNI/VISCII conversion machinery
                     (charset.cpp/data.cpp/convert.cpp) is dropped, not vendored.
  - charset_utf8.cpp the UTF-8 emitter + StdVnToUpper/Lower + VnConvert stub.
  - vnlexi_tables.cpp  the VnLexiName->Unicode codepoint table and the
                     no-tone / root fold tables. GENERATED by gen_tables.py from
                     the self-documenting VnLexiName names (vnl_ar1 = a+roof+tone1)
                     plus the Unicode standard — i.e. reconstructed clean-room, NOT
                     copied out of the GPL data.cpp/charset.cpp.
  - mactab_stub.cpp  no-op CMacroTable (macros/gõ tắt disabled in the PoC; the
                     upstream mactab.cpp is GPL-coupled via vnconv).
  - gen_tables.py    the table generator (kept so the tables are reproducible).
  - poc_driver.cc    host-side test harness. NOT part of the Chrome build.

Build knobs (mandatory): compile with -funsigned-char (the engine indexes tables
with char). No exceptions/RTTI are used. Productionization path (per
VIETNAMESE-IME-PERF.md §3.3): build ukengine as libukengine.so and dlopen it in
the IME service to quarantine the LGPL relink obligation, mirroring libimedecoder.
